      "_guide": "Ranked by the FORWARD/sustainable dividend yield (dividend.yield_pct) unless order_by=streak|cagr. DON'T judge yield alone — DECOMPOSE it: (a) if yield_trailing_pct >> yield_pct a SPECIAL/one-time dividend inflated the trailing figure (not a repeatable income) — quote the forward yield_pct; (b) payout_ratio > 1 = paying out MORE than it earns (unsustainable, cut risk); (c) a high yield from a PRICE drop (near week52_low, news.net_direction=neg) + intact/growing dividend (ttm_div_yoy_pct up, positive cagr_5y_pct, no_cut_streak_yrs at its 10 ceiling) = possible VALUE, but a recent last_cut_year + negative ttm_div_yoy_pct + high payout + bad news = TRAP. no_cut_streak_yrs is a bounded RELIABILITY signal — consecutive no-cut years within a 10-YEAR window, CAPPED at 10 (10 = clean through the whole decade incl. 2020 & 2022 stress). It is NOT the dividend's full age: do NOT state a multi-decade 'aristocrat/king' streak from prior knowledge — say 'clean for 10y+ (the full tracked window)'. Explain the WHY from news.top_reason. Research-analyst voice — observations, not advice.",
