  "answer_to_user": "I ranked by 5-year dividend growth (CAGR) rather than current yield, so these are payers whose dividend is actually rising. Fastest growers in the screen: Shenzhen Batian Ecotypic (002170.CS) ~136% 5y CAGR, freenet AG (FNTN.XETRA, Germany) ~118%, B'IN Live (6625.TW) ~115%, Tetragon Financial (TFGS.LSE) ~112%, Jiangsu Zhengdan Chemical (300641.CS) ~97%, and Powertip Image (6498.TWO) ~88%. Two honest caveats. First, the classic trade-off: strong dividend growers often start at a LOWER current yield (they compound income over time) rather than paying a fat static yield today — though several here happen to pay ~6-9% now. Second, and important: this CAGR and the no-cut 'streak' are measured over a ~10-year tracked window at most — I can see 5-year growth and up to a 10-year no-cut streak, but I cannot verify multi-decade growth records. Note also that some of these have a payout ratio above 1 (Shenzhen Batian ~1.40, freenet ~1.01, Jiangsu Zhengdan ~1.31), meaning the dividend currently exceeds earnings — fast recent growth off a low base isn't the same as a sustainable, sustainably-growing dividend. So treat this as 'who has grown the dividend within the years I can see,' pair it with payout sustainability, and don't read it as a guaranteed forward growth streak."
